| The forge contract (#6191): one scripted sequence (a pull request opens, a check fails, a check passes, a conflict, a review asks for changes, a comment, a merge, a close, a refused call; for a tracker, an issue opens, is commented, assigned, labelled and closed, and a refused call) and the events each step must raise, with `pr.blocked`'s reasons, the same for every forge server. Which of the contract's events each server gives: **github** all nine (`pr.opened`, `checks.failed`, `pr.blocked` with every reason, `checks.passed`, `pr.conflicted`, `pr.reviewed`, `pr.commented`, `pr.merged`, `pr.closed`); **gitlab** all but `checks.passed`, `pr.reviewed` and `pr.commented` (#6296); **forgejo** all but `checks.passed`, `pr.reviewed` and `pr.commented`, and its `pr.blocked` gives only `conflict` (#6294); **bitbucket** all nine, with `pr.blocked`'s `conflict`, `required_check_failed` and `changes_requested` (#6293); **azuredevops** all nine, with `pr.blocked`'s `conflict`, `required_check_failed` and `changes_requested` (#6295); **linear** and **azureboards** all five issue events; **jira** all but `issue.closed` (#6297). A refused call (429 or 401) is an error on every server, never an empty list | agents | built, tested with fakes | Events | 2026-11-19, against each server's fake (`TestForgeContract` in each package's `contract_test.go`) | `Go/internal/forgecontract/contract.go`, `Go/internal/*mcp/contract_test.go` | the live mode (`forgecontract.Live`, `-tags live`) is run on real accounts by #3739 (Codeberg), #3771 (Bitbucket Cloud) and #3782 (Azure DevOps); the missing events and reasons are #6294 to #6297 |
